          "text": [
            "Llama.generate: prefix-match hit\n"
          ]
        },
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "'\\nAccording to Merck Manuals, a fracture is a break in a bone. A fractured leg can occur due to various reasons, including falls or hiking accidents. The following are the necessary precautions and treatment steps for a person who has fractured their leg during a hiking trip:\\n1. Immobilize the affected leg: Use a splint, sling, or cast to prevent any movement of the bone fragments. This will help reduce pain, prevent further damage, and promote healing.\\n2. Apply ice: Apply an ice pack to the affected area for 15-20 minutes at a time, several times a day, to reduce swelling and pain.\\n3. Elevate the leg: Keep the leg elevated above heart level to help reduce swelling and prevent further damage to the surrounding tissues.\\n4. Pain relief: Use over-the-counter pain relievers such as acetaminophen or ibuprofen to manage pain. Prescription pain medication may be necessary in some cases.\\n5. Seek medical attention: It is important to seek medical attention as soon as possible for proper diagnosis and treatment. The healthcare provider may recommend X-rays, splinting, casting, or surgery depending on the severity of the fracture.\\n6. Follow-up care: Attend all follow-up appointments with the healthcare provider to monitor progress and ensure proper healing. Physical therapy may be necessary to help restore strength and mobility to the affected leg.\\n7. Considerations for care and recovery: The person should avoid putting weight on the affected leg until it has healed completely. They should also avoid smoking, as it can delay healing. Proper nutrition and hydration are essential for promoting healing and preventing complications such as infection or blood clots. Additionally, they should be encouraged to maintain a positive attitude and engage in activities that do not put undue stress on the affected leg during recovery.'"
            ],
            "application/vnd.google.colaboratory.intrinsic+json": {
              "type": "string"
            }
          },
